<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikolai Yudenich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1862–1933</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikolai Yudenich was a Russian general who won notable victories against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, including the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzurum">Erzurum</a> in 1916. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a> he led the White North-Western Army from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> in an offensive on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> in October 1919, which was repulsed. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikolai-yudenich.jpg" alt="Nikolai Yudenich" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Сканирование: Владимир Васильев · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nikolai_N._Yudenich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
